#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""hearth-wallpaper: the wallpaper engine's worker (services/Wallpaper.qml).

Everything slow or networked runs here, in a separate process, so the shell's
UI thread never waits: picture-of-the-day providers, downloads, smart crops,
dynamic-wallpaper schedules (GNOME XML, macOS .heic, hearth's dynamic.json),
Wallpaper Engine project scans, video posters, Shadertoy compiles, API keys
and the lock/login-screen export. Each command prints one JSON object (or
array) on stdout; errors print {"error": "..."} and exit 1.

  hearth-wallpaper fetch SOURCE --dir CACHE [--opts JSON] [--offset N] [--min WxH]
  hearth-wallpaper crop SRC W H OUT
  hearth-wallpaper dynamic PATH --dir CACHE [--index N] [--lat L --lon L]
  hearth-wallpaper scan-dynamic DIR...
  hearth-wallpaper scan-we [--steam] [DIR...]   --steam: find Steam libraries too
  hearth-wallpaper scan-media DIR...          videos and pictures (for the grid)
  hearth-wallpaper scan-folder DIR [--recursive]
  hearth-wallpaper poster VIDEO OUT
  hearth-wallpaper shader SRC OUT              Shadertoy mainImage() -> .qsb
  hearth-wallpaper secret get|set|delete NAME  (set reads the value on stdin)
  hearth-wallpaper export JSONFILE [--data JSON] [--system DIR]
"""

